            <ArticleTitle>Computed tomography in low-back-pain after femur-amputation for osteogenic sarcoma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>164-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Following amputation of a lower extremity for osteogenic sarcoma, the lumbar muscles receive an asymmetric strain. This predisposes to low-back-pain. When this occurs, tumour-recurrence must be excluded. This report demonstrates the usefulness of high-resolution computed tomography (CT) in this clinical situation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
